## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of multi-environment deployments without code duplication using provider aliases and module iteration.

## Key Concepts
- Provider aliases
- Module instantiation with for_each
- Per-environment variable files and backends
- Terraform plan/apply targeting to avoid cross-env changes

## Code Example
```terraform
provider "aws" {
  alias  = "prod"
  region = var.prod_region
}
provider "aws" {
  alias  = "dev"
  region = var.dev_region
}
variable "prod_region" { default = "us-east-1" }
variable "dev_region"  { default = "us-west-2" }
variable "environments" {
  type = map(string)
  default = { prod = "prod", dev = "dev" }
}
module "network" {
  for_each = var.environments
  source   = "./modules/network"
  providers = { aws = aws[each.value] }
  # inputs per env
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you add a new environment without touching existing state?
- What are the trade-offs of using separate backends versus workspaces for this pattern?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to compose remote state across envs, leverage backend aliases, and isolate region-specific DNS resources. Also assesses practical CI gating to prevent prod drift.

## Key Concepts
- Backend aliases and per-env state
- terraform_remote_state data source for cross-env outputs
- for_each with a DNS map to generate records
- CI gating with plan JSON to block prod changes

## Code Example
```hcl
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket = "tfstate-bucket"
    key    = "envs/region-eu/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "eu-west-1"
  }
}

data "terraform_remote_state" "prod" {
  backend = "s3"
  config = {
    bucket = "tfstate-bucket"
    key    = "envs/prod/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}

module "dns" {
  source       = "./modules/dns"
  dns_records  = var.dns_records
  prod_zone_id = data.terraform_remote_state.prod.outputs.zone_id
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this to 5 regions while keeping drift detection?
- How do you handle secrets in backend configs for multi-tenant regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of remote state isolation, cross-env data sharing, and basic CI gating for beginner Terraform workflows.

## Key Concepts
- terraform_remote_state data source
- backend alias and per-env state keys
- var-files for environment specificity (qa.tfvars)
- CI gating with plan validation before apply

## Code Example
```javascript
// qa backend example (HCL in Terraform syntax, shown as JS for formatting)
terraform {
  backend "s3" {
    bucket         = "my-terraform-state"
    key            = "envs/qa/terraform.tfstate"
    region         = "us-east-1"
    dynamodb_table = "tf-locks"
  }
}

data "terraform_remote_state" "prod" {
  backend = "s3"
  config = {
    bucket = "my-terraform-state"
    key    = "envs/prod/terraform.tfstate"
    region = "us-east-1"
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-region VPCs?
- How would you test for drift between prod and qa after apply?
